CPU binary ops (ADD / SUB / MUL / DIV): when src1 holds one value per row (ne10 == 1, a per-channel bias or scale
broadcast over [W, H, C] activations, as in every VAE conv bias add and group-norm affine), apply it to the whole row
in one loop. The contiguous-rows path split such a row into ne00 / ne10 = W calls of vec_binary_op_contiguous with
n = 1 (vDSP with length 1 under Accelerate), one call per element. Same op on the same operands per element, so the
result is bit-identical.

